# TypeScript coding style

Applies to `apps/web` only. `apps/web/AGENTS.md` wins on Next.js APIs. The always-on security rule wins on secrets and embed behavior.

## Updates

Copy objects instead of mutating a value the caller still holds:

```typescript
function renameUser(user: User, name: string): User {
  return { ...user, name };
}
```

Do not spread untrusted JSON into state. Keep only known fields.

## Errors

Await async work and handle the failure. Do not log the raw error when it might contain a secret, token, or vault material. Surface the existing problem shape used in `apps/web/src/lib` instead of inventing a new error string.

## Validation

Validate input and reject unknown fields. Use the parsers already in `apps/web/src/lib`. Do not add a new validation dependency for a single change.

## Logging

Do not commit `console.log` in product paths. Never log secrets, session cookies, PEM, or vault material.
